## Method
Built with `ws_build`/`ws_serve` from .swarm/tier3/lib/common.sh (nice -n 19,
GOMAXPROCS=4, one server at a time, isolated port, never :8080) against the
snapshot at scratchpad/snap/WS5.5-a11y, fixture built with
`python3 .swarm/tier3/WS5/make_fixture.py` (Alex Primary 1958-11 primary, Sam
Spouse 1971-08 spouse linked to a healthcare entry + an unlinked third
person, start_date 2026-09, glide_path {enabled:false}). Two lanes:
1. A Playwright driver (chromium, NODE_PATH per common.sh) that (a) POSTs
   directly the way the oracle's probe.js does — empty birth month with a
   quoted name (`Robert "Bob" Smith`), an unparseable five-digit-year month
   with a backslash name (`Pat\X`, "19711-08"), an HTML-tag name (`<b>x</b>`),
   the after-start-date case, and an invalid start date ("20266-09") — and
   inspects the raw wire text; (b) drives the real UI (`input[type=month]`
   .fill("19711-08") + change event, `#projection-start-date` value set +
   change) in both themes (localStorage theme + documentElement.classList,
   matching base.js's own toggle, matching WS5.4's method); (c) walks D6/D7;
   (d) injects axe-core 4.13 (same build @axe-core/cli ships) via
   page.evaluate at baseline + each error state, both themes.
2. `axe` CLI (@axe-core/cli, on PATH) run against two throwaway static wraps
   (light, and `<html class="dark">`) that embed the LIVE server's own raw
   response bytes for the unparseable-birth-month fragment (curl'd from the
   running isolated server, not hand-built HTML) and load the snapshot's
   real built web/static/css/tailwind.css + styles.css.
Server killed after each run (ws_stop via the sourced trap, confirmed no
stray process/tmp dir afterward); `ps aux`/`git status --short` on both the
agents2 worktree and /home/darrell/bin/ai/budget2 show no changes and no
:8080 contact; grepped my own scripts for "8080" — none.

## 1. Message-as-rendered checks (point 5, point 6, WS5 rulings 2026-09-24g/i)
Raw wire text (direct POST, decoded entities for readability):
- empty month, quoted name: `Robert "Bob" Smith needs a birth month`
- unparseable, backslash name: `Pat\X's birth month "19711-08" isn't a
  valid month (use YYYY-MM)`
- HTML-tag name: `<b>x</b> needs a birth month` — wire bytes are
  `&lt;b&gt;x&lt;/b&gt; needs a birth month`, no live `<b>` tag in the
  response (confirmed by regex on raw bytes).
- after-start: `Future Kid's birth month (2030-01) is after the plan's
  start date (2026-09)` — never "needs a birth month".
- invalid start date: `Invalid projection start date: invalid month
  "20266-09"` — never "Invalid person data".
All PASS: correct wording per shape, names the person, states the value/
format (YYYY-MM) in text. Wire encoding is exactly one html.EscapeString
pass (`&#34;`, `&#39;`, `&lt;`/`&gt;`) — no raw backslash-escape leftovers
(`\"`) and no double-escaped entities (`&amp;#34;`) found in any of the
four responses. Live DOM textContent (UI-triggered) shows real apostrophes/
quotes, not entities — AT reads plain readable text, confirmed both themes.

## 2. Announcement (point 5) — role/aria-live, single instance
Both themes, UI-triggered unparseable-month: exactly one `[role="alert"]`
node exists at a time (renderError's own markup, reused verbatim by
base.js's buildErrorNode — never re-wrapped or duplicated); text matches
the new message; clearing back to a valid value removes the alert (0 nodes)
— confirmed for both the unparseable-month and (via D7's pre-existing
linked-removal-refusal alert, unregressed) the healthcare-refusal path.
`role="alert"` implies an implicit assertive live region per the ARIA spec
that AT honors without a separate `aria-live` attribute — same mechanism
WS4/WS5.2-4 already established and PASSed; unchanged here.

## 3. Contrast, both themes (point 7)
Reused, unchanged renderError classes (`text-negative` on `bg-negative-
soft`): light fg rgb(190,18,60) / bg rgb(255,241,242); dark fg
rgb(253,164,175) / bg rgb(41,23,42) — same computed colors WS5.4 measured
(5.72:1 light / 8.88:1 dark, both > 4.5:1). axe-core confirms 0
color-contrast violations on the alert's own nodes in either theme (both
the live-page scan and the static tailwind.css-loaded wrap of the live
server's own unparseable-month response bytes).

## 4. Focus (point 9)
Both themes: after the UI-triggered error, `document.activeElement` is
still the edited `#person-birth-month-<id>` input — unchanged from WS5.4's
established behaviour (no focus move to the alert, consistent with
ACCESSIBILITY.md point 5's "or an aria-live region announces" branch, since
role=alert is exactly that live-region announcement).

